Data
----

The base pack (basepack/, built by tools/packager; see
docs/data/base-pack.md) contains:

Blue Marble Next Generation with topography and bathymetry (July 2004)
  NASA Earth Observatory (Reto Stöckli and others)
  Licence: public domain (NASA); credit requested
  Attribution: "Blue Marble: NASA Earth Observatory"
  https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/blue-marble-next-generation/

GSHHG 2.3.7 (Global Self-consistent, Hierarchical, High-resolution
Geography Database), resolutions c, l and i, cut to tiles
  Paul Wessel (University of Hawaii) and Walter H. F. Smith (NOAA)
  Licence: GNU LGPL v3 or later; the licence texts (LICENSE.TXT,
  COPYING.LESSERv3, gpl-3.0.txt) are in basepack/licences/gshhg/
  Attribution: "Shoreline: GSHHG 2.3.7, P. Wessel and W. H. F. Smith (LGPL)"
  Source: https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/gshhg-gmt/releases/tag/2.3.7
  The program that turns it into the pack's form is tools/packager in
  this source tree.

Natural Earth 1:10m Cultural Vectors, Admin 0 – Countries, version 5.1.2,
widened by about 5 km and simplified
  Natural Earth (naturalearthdata.com)
  Licence: public domain; credit requested
  Attribution: "Countries: Made with Natural Earth"
  Source: https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/tree/v5.1.2

The source tree also has test data that is not distributed:
tests/data/geodtest-sample.dat, a sample of C. F. F. Karney's "Test set
for geodesics", CC0 1.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.32156.

